------------------------------------------------------------------------------
PARITY SCOPE  (Honesty #2 No-scope-narrowing)
------------------------------------------------------------------------------
The web <DataTable> is a PROP-DRIVEN presentational component: its data arrives as the `data: T[]` prop — there
is NO fetch, NO React-Query cache, NO Promise — so it has NO loading / stale / offline branch (the hosting page
owns those and feeds `data` down). Inventing that chrome would FABRICATE states the source lacks, so this
surface reproduces only the source's REAL branches — the same disposition the accepted sibling presentational
primitives DataTableBulkBar (0209), DataTableResizer (0212), and Pagination (0221) used. The REAL branches, all
reproduced + previewed + tested:
  • populated : the rows (standard + lazily-windowed via LazyVStack — the native peer of useVirtualizer).
  • empty     : data.isEmpty -> the emptyMessage row (web `data.length === 0`).
  • error     : the SectionErrorBoundary "This table failed to render" fallback, reached on a host-signalled
                failure OR a duplicate-key collision (the native peer of React's "two children with the same
                key"), with a retry affordance (the web boundary auto-retries on re-render).
Plus every interactive feature the source renders: sort (+chevron/aria-sort), single/multi selection (checkbox
/radio, select-all + indeterminate, macOS shift-range), expandable row drawers, per-column resize, column
visibility + drag-reorder (+ the ↑/↓ menu), CSV export, pagination, mobile column hiding, density, and the row
context menu.
Data sources : useTranslation -> the P1/S10 DataTableStrings facade; useVirtualizer -> SwiftUI LazyVStack
               (inherent row windowing); useSortToggle -> the controlled sortKey/sortDirection + onSort
               (DataTableSortDirection.toggled is the verbatim `d === 'asc' ? 'desc' : 'asc'`).
Composed     : the toolbar/footer/resize children are EACH their own prompt (Out of Scope: "Other surfaces in
               the same feature") and are COMPOSED as the real architecture: DataTableBulkBar (0209),
               DataTableColumnMenu (0210) + its controller, DataTableResizer (0212), PaginationView (0221) +
               its controller. The shared pure ColumnLayout / ColumnDescriptor / ColumnLayoutProjector (the
               native port of lib/columnOrderStore) are reused for ordering (DRY). The prompt's "Shared
               components used: (none)" refers to atomic shared components (Button/Badge/…) — DataTable uses
               raw HTML elements on the web, so none; the four full surfaces above are composed integration
               points, not atomic components.
Charts/maps  : none (the web source uses none) -> Swift Charts / MapKit not required.
i18n keys    : errors.section.tableTitle, table.selection.deselectRow/selectRow/deselectAll/selectAll,
               table.expand.collapse/expand/column, table.export.csv/csvButton, table.columns.resizeLabel —
               ALL resolved through the P1/S10 facade; + native table.empty.default / table.error.retry. No
               English literals in code.
Telemetry    : view.opened emitted once with slug "DataTable" (P1/S11).
a11y         : VoiceOver labels on every interactive element (row checkbox/radio, select-all, expand chevron,
               sort button + spoken sort value, resize handle, export, column menu, pager); the row checkbox
               carries the .isSelected trait; Dynamic Type via the type tokens; the resizer/menu fades honor
               Reduce Motion (inherited from the composed surfaces).

